📄 UserRepository.java
1. Purpose
Repository is the Data Access Layer (DAO).
It is responsible for interacting with the database.
We don't write SQL for basic CRUD operations because Spring Data JPA provides them.
2. Code
@Repository
public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {

}
3. Annotations & Classes
@Repository

Purpose

Marks this interface as the Repository layer.
Spring detects it as a Bean and manages it in the IoC container.
Also translates database exceptions into Spring's DataAccessException.
JpaRepository<User, Long>

Purpose

Provides ready-made CRUD methods.
No implementation is needed.

User

Entity class.

Long

Type of the Primary Key (id).
4. Built-in Methods
save(entity)

