Interview Questions
Q1. What is Repository?

Repository is the Data Access Layer responsible for performing database operations.

Q2. Why do we extend JpaRepository?

Because it already provides built-in CRUD operations like save(), findById(), findAll(), and deleteById(), reducing boilerplate code.

Q3. Why is UserRepository an interface and not a class?

Spring Data JPA automatically generates the implementation at runtime using proxies, so we only define the interface.

Q4. What does JpaRepository<User, Long> mean?
User → Entity class.
Long → Type of the primary key.
Q5. Who implements JpaRepository methods?

Spring Data JPA generates the implementation automatically at runtime.

Q6. Do we write SQL for CRUD operations?

No. Spring Data JPA generates the SQL automatically.

Q7. Can we create custom methods without writing SQL?

Yes. Spring Data JPA derives queries from method names, for example:

findByEmail(String email)
Q8. What is the difference between CrudRepository, PagingAndSortingRepository, and JpaRepository?
CrudRepository → Basic CRUD operations.
PagingAndSortingRepository → CRUD + Pagination & Sorting.
JpaRepository → Everything above + JPA-specific features like flush(), batch operations, etc.

Interview Tip: Most Spring Boot projects use JpaRepository.

Key Points to Remember
Repository = Database layer.
Extends JpaRepository.
